module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_field_default_is_evaluated_in_the_callers_scope

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { NoRungStated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_field_default_is_evaluated_in_the_callers_scope: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_field_default_is_evaluated_in_the_callers_scope" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: NoRungStated },

  receipts: [
    "a field default is evaluated in the CALLER'S environment, not the declaring module's. A field whose default expression references a constructor (or any name) bound only in the declaring module fails with NoSuchVariable at every call site that omits that field. The caller sees no diagnostic connecting the failure to the default; the variable name is all the error carries. The declaring module compiled clean, the operation declaration typechecked, and the failure is invisible until the operation is CALLED without that argument.",

    "SPECIMEN, found 2026-11-09 (heal-publish run 42677477262, PR #16176, regression from #16160). dag/extdeps/cloud/gcp/sts.dag declares `subject_token_type: SubjectTokenType = Jwt` and `requested_token_type: RequestedTokenType = RequestAccessToken` in the Exchange operation's input block. Jwt and RequestAccessToken are nullary constructors of types declared in the same sts.dag module. dag/gunbc/heal_publication.dag imports the module as a whole (`import extdeps.cloud.gcp.sts`) without a named-import list, so Jwt is NOT bound in heal_publication's scope. When heal_publication_publish_wet calls gcp.STS.Exchange without subject_token_type, the interpreter's call_function_inner evaluates the default expression `Jwt` in the CALLER's env (v1_interpreter.rs line 8419: eval_expr(default_node, env, ctx) where env is the caller's environment) and raises NoSuchVariable{Jwt}. Every heal-publish candidate on every PR fails.",

    "THE LANGUAGE-LAYER DEFECT: this is a scoping violation at the evaluator level. Field defaults are part of the operation's declaration and their names should resolve in the declaring module's scope. The evaluator instead threads the caller's environment, coupling every operation's defaults to what its callers happen to import. The consequence is a fragility class: any default expression that references an unexported or differently-scoped name fails at every call site that omits the field, with a misleading NoSuchVariable naming a constructor the caller has never seen.",

    "THE INTERIM REMEDY (this hotfix, #16183): import the constructors by name at the call site's module AND pass them explicitly, so the default is never evaluated. This is per-call-site, does not fix the class, and leaves every other default built from an unimported constructor latent for the next caller to trip over.",

    "THE PROPER FIX (language layer, NOT in this hotfix): v1_interpreter.rs call_function_inner should evaluate field defaults in the declaring module's environment (resolved from fn_node's module binding), not the caller's env. A claim would need to demonstrate that a constructor visible ONLY in the declaring module is reachable via a default at a caller that does not import it."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
